\f1\fs22 Sarah stared out the window of her private quarters at Sublime Point, her view stretching over verdant valleys that would have been breathtaking under other circumstances. Now, her mind was occupied with calculations and contingencies.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"I can't believe that bastard Dunhilton," she muttered, pressing her palm against the glass. "Using a designer virus to slaughter innocent people."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kathy looked up from her tablet, where she'd been reviewing Sarah's latest prenatal scans. "The death toll is still rising. Over three hundred confirmed Elvi casualties so far."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"And it would be thousands more if not for..." Sarah trailed off, a thought crystallizing. She turned abruptly. "Kathy, have you done any follow-up examinations on Tony recently?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Last month," Kathy replied, setting down her tablet. "Why?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Have you noticed how... vigorous he looks? Like he hasn't aged a day since we met?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley, sprawled on Sarah's couch reviewing security protocols, perked up. "Now that you mention it, he looked absurdly healthy during the joint venture ceremony. I assumed it was makeup or lighting for the cameras."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"It's not makeup," Sarah said carefully. "It's something else. Something biological."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kathy's medical instincts engaged immediately. "Are you suggesting Tony has some kind of... immunity to the TMinus-Virus?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Not just immunity," Sarah said, pacing now. "Enhanced health. Resilience. The TMinus-Virus is killing Elvi all over the city, but I'd bet anything that Tony's recent... companions are completely unaffected."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley sat up straight. "You think he's spreading some kind of counter-agent?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"I think," Sarah said slowly, "we should investigate that possibility."\
