\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The High Elvis received them in his headquarters\'97formerly the Memphis Mafia Bar, now decorated with Evolution Elvi iconography and Richard Dawkins quotes alongside traditional Elvis memorabilia. His security detail wore blindingly sequined ponchos with what appeared to be decorative guitars slung over their shoulders that were quite clearly weapons.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Across the street stood a competing establishment\'97a former nightclub now renamed "The King's Gospel House," where Pastor Rex Humble led his breakaway faction of Gospel Elvi. The religious schism was visible in the contrasting decorations: scientific formulas versus biblical verses rendered in neon.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"The Holy Momma graces us with her presence," the High Elvis intoned, bowing deeply. "What brings you to our humble quarter while the plague of Dunhilton torments us?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As Hayley presented their findings about Tony's apparent viral immunity, the High Elvis's expression shifted from concern to calculating interest to barely contained excitement.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Let me understand," he said, leaning forward eagerly. "The Great Teacher's... intimate partners are immune to the virus? And this immunity spreads?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Yes," Kathy confirmed. "We've documented at least three generations of transmission, each providing complete protection."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The High Elvis's eyes gleamed. "This is a sign! The great Dawkins working through the Great Teacher, bestowing evolutionary advantage upon the faithful!"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"It's a health crisis," Hayley corrected firmly, "requiring organized intervention."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Of course, of course," the High Elvis nodded, already calculating. "A mass inoculation event. A celebration of Evolution Elvi superiority over our misguided Gospel brethren."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"This isn't about your religious feud," Sarah cautioned. "It's about saving lives."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Naturally," the High Elvis agreed too quickly. "We must consult the Great Teacher immediately. His wisdom guides all important decisions."\
