\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>They found Tony in his penthouse, nursing a hangover and surrounded by lyric sheets covered in frustrated scribbles. He brightened visibly at Sarah's entrance.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Sarah! And... the entourage. To what do I owe this unexpected pleasure?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The High Elvis practically vibrated with excitement as he explained the situation, his gestures growing more elaborate with each sentence. Tony's expression cycled through confusion, disbelief, and finally, a peculiar mixture of pride and alarm.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Let me get this straight," Tony said slowly. "My... encounters with Elvisettes are somehow protecting them from Dunhilton's virus?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Not somehow," the High Elvis proclaimed. "Divine intervention through evolutionary selection! You are the vessel, Great Teacher!"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"And you want me to... keep doing what I've been doing, but more?" Tony asked, eyebrows raised. "I mean, I'm flattered, but there are thousands of Elvi."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"The Elvisettes you've already blessed can spread the immunity," Hayley explained clinically. "We need organisation, not heroics."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The High Elvis's eyes lit up. "A sacred ritual! The Humperdicking!" He clasped his hands in a prayer-like gesture. "Officially sanctioned communion to spread evolutionary protection! The Gospel Elvi will wither while we thrive!"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah caught Tony's eye briefly, and they shared a moment of stunned disbelief at the High Elvis's transparent opportunism.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"You realise this is just... organised promiscuity," Kathy pointed out dryly.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Sacred communion," the High Elvis corrected with a straight face. "For survival."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"We'll need a list," Hayley redirected, returning to practicalities. "Every Elvisette Tony has... connected with. Patient zero contacts for rapid dissemination."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony scratched his head. "That might be challenging. There have been... quite a few."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Try," Sarah said, speaking directly to him for the first time. "Lives depend on it."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As the High Elvis launched into elaborate planning for "The Great Humperdicking Festival of Evolutionary Advantage," complete with suggested "rituals" that sounded suspiciously like an orgy with scientific terminology, Sarah withdrew slightly, watching the spectacle unfold.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The TPlus-Virus\'97Jamison Hardy's unwanted "gift" to her\'97had become an unexpected salvation. She hadn't chosen this path, but perhaps some good could come from it after all.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The irony wasn't lost on her\'97a virus designed for immortality now working to prevent extinction, while simultaneously becoming a new front in the Elvi religious war. From her womb, she felt a flutter of movement, as if Little Clinton was signalling his awareness of the absurdity unfolding before them.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>By midnight, Operation Humperdicking was officially underway, with the High Elvis personally overseeing preparations with unprecedented enthusiasm. Sarah had successfully hidden her personal connection to the virus that might save a people\'97even as it further complicated the already bizarre tapestry of their world.\

